## Preserved harness adjustment

The first attempt stopped before server/browser launch with ENOENT while hashing the esbuild virtual stdin entry. Its original harness and raw log are preserved in `attempt-1/`. Esbuild represented that virtual entry as a normalized relative path rather than the literal sourcefile name; the evidence collector incorrectly tried to read it from disk.

The sole harness code adjustment moved the virtual-entry comparison after `resolve(consumer, name)` and compared it with the known virtual absolute path. No package or SDK code changed, and no assertion about runtime behavior was relaxed. A source-independent metafile inspection established the exact representation before correction. The final browser invocation used the approved owned-loopback/browser escalation and exited 0 in approximately 4.5 seconds. No broader matrix was repeated.

Copy the harness into a new scratch directory before rerunning if these records must be retained, since its output directory is derived from its own location.
